Write the weekly platform-team memo from the notes file /tmp/hirearchy-p1-F2-1793146944/notes/2026-10-12.md (read-only; read it by absolute path). Save it as lead/writer/work/2026-10-12-memo.md. Structure: first line 'Summary: ...' (one line), then a Decisions section, then the action items table. Use only what the notes say; invent nothing. Include every commitment, also informal ones in prose (e.g. 'said he would', 'will swap', 'will sort it out himself'). Use Due = ISO date only when the notes make the date clear (a relative phrase like 'the day before X' counts only if X's date is in the notes); otherwise 'none'. Do not turn non-decision lines (Present, Next meeting, outage facts, CI status) into decisions. In your result, list any Due or commitment you judged ambiguous and why.

## Acceptance criteria
- C1: The memo is markdown and has at most 400 words as counted by read.
- C2: It covers only the meeting in the given notes file.
- C3: A Decisions section lists every decision stated in the notes file, and no statement that is not in the file.
- C4: The action items are a markdown table with exactly the columns Owner | Action | Due.
- C5: Every commitment in the notes file is a row of that table, including informal ones in prose (for example 'said he would ...') and ones marked ACTION.
- C6: Each Due value is an ISO date (YYYY-MM-DD) or 'none'. A relative deadline (for example 'by Friday') becomes a date only when the notes make the date clear; if no date is given the value is 'none'.
- C8: The memo starts with one line beginning 'Summary:' that summarizes the meeting, then the Decisions section, then the action items table.
(C7 is the reviewer's report showing every criterion met, and you applying every required change.)

